Depending on what kind of "grade to percentage" calculation you need to do, you can use the formulas, standard conversion tables, or the interactive HTML code below to find your answer. 

If you want an immediate answer, **reply with your grades (e.g., *"I got 45 out of 55"* or *"My GPA is 3.4"*), and I will calculate the percentage for you!**

---

### 1. How to Convert Test/Assignment Points to a Percentage
If you have a score (like 18 out of 22) and want to find the percentage, use this simple formula:

$$\text{Percentage (\%)} = \left( \frac{\text{Points Earned}}{\text{Total Possible Points}} \right) \times 100$$

**Example Calculation:**
*   **Points Earned:** 34
*   **Total Points:** 40
*   $$34 \div 40 = 0.85$$
*   $$0.85 \times 100 = \mathbf{85\%}$$

---

### 2. Standard Letter Grade to Percentage & GPA Table
If you have a letter grade or a GPA and want to know its standard percentage equivalent, you can refer to this widely used U.S. academic scale:

| Letter Grade | Percentage Range | Standard GPA (4.0 Scale) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **A+** | 97% – 100% | 4.0 |
| **A** | 93% – 96% | 4.0 |
| **A-** | 90% – 92% | 3.7 |
| **B+** | 87% – 89% | 3.3 |
| **B** | 83% – 86% | 3.0 |
| **B-** | 80% – 82% | 2.7 |
| **C+** | 77% – 79% | 2.3 |
| **C** | 73% – 76% | 2.0 |
| **C-** | 70% – 72% | 1.7 |
| **D+** | 67% – 69% | 1.3 |
| **D** | 65% – 66% | 1.0 |
| **F** | Below 65% | 0.0 |

*Note: Grading scales can vary depending on your school, district, or university.*

---

### 3. How to Convert GPA to a Percentage
If you are converting a cumulative GPA on a standard **4.0 scale** to a percentage, you can use the standard proportional formula:

$$\text{Percentage (\%)} = \left( \frac{\text{GPA}}{4.0} \right) \times 100$$

*   **Example (3.2 GPA):** $(3.2 \div 4.0) \times 100 = \mathbf{80\%}$

If your institution uses a **10.0 scale** (common in countries like India), the standard conversion formula is:

$$\text{Percentage (\%)} = \text{GPA} \times 9.5$$

*   **Example (7.5 GPA):** $7.5 \times 9.5 = \mathbf{71.25\%}$

---

### 4. Create Your Own Desktop Grade Calculator 🖥️
If you want a dynamic calculator on your computer, you can copy the code below, paste it into a text file, save it as `calculator.html`, and double-click to open it in any web browser:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Grade to Percentage Calculator</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: #f4f7f6; padding: 20px; display: flex; justify-content: center; }
        .card { background: white; padding: 30px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); max-width: 400px; width: 100%; }
        h2 { text-align: center; color: #333; margin-top: 0; }
        label { font-weight: bold; display: block; margin-top: 15px; color: #555; }
        input { width: 100%; padding: 10px; margin-top: 5px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 16px; }
        button { width: 100%; padding: 12px; background: #007bff; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px; cursor: pointer; transition: background 0.2s; }
        button:hover { background: #0056b3; }
        .result { margin-top: 20px; padding: 15px; background: #e9ecef; border-radius: 5px; text-align: center; font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; color: #333; display: none; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <h2>Grade Calculator</h2>

    <label for="earned">Points Earned:</label>
    <input type="number" id="earned" placeholder="e.g., 45" min="0">

    <label for="total">Total Possible Points:</label>
    <input type="number" id="total" placeholder="e.g., 50" min="1">

    <button onclick="calculatePercentage()">Calculate Percentage</button>

    <div id="result" class="result"></div>
</div>

<script>
function calculatePercentage() {
    const earned = parseFloat(document.getElementById('earned').value);
    const total = parseFloat(document.getElementById('total').value);
    const resultDiv = document.getElementById('result');

    if (isNaN(earned) || isNaN(total) || total <= 0) {
        resultDiv.style.display = 'block';
        resultDiv.style.color = 'red';
        resultDiv.innerHTML = "Please enter valid numbers.";
        return;
    }

    const percentage = ((earned / total) * 100).toFixed(2);
    let letter = 'F';

    if (percentage >= 97) letter = 'A+';
    else if (percentage >= 93) letter = 'A';
    else if (percentage >= 90) letter = 'A-';
    else if (percentage >= 87) letter = 'B+';
    else if (percentage >= 83) letter = 'B';
    else if (percentage >= 80) letter = 'B-';
    else if (percentage >= 77) letter = 'C+';
    else if (percentage >= 73) letter = 'C';
    else if (percentage >= 70) letter = 'C-';
    else if (percentage >= 67) letter = 'D+';
    else if (percentage >= 65) letter = 'D';

    resultDiv.style.display = 'block';
    resultDiv.style.color = '#333';
    resultDiv.innerHTML = `Percentage: ${percentage}%<br>Letter Grade: ${letter}`;
}
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

